# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local data location for the building consents project
#
# 1. Copy this file to `.Renviron` in the same folder (building-consents/):
#        cp .Renviron.example .Renviron
# 2. Set STAT462_DATA to the folder that holds the Stats NZ CSVs on YOUR
#    machine. It is searched recursively, so the folder you unzipped the
#    downloads into is enough (sub-folders are fine).
# 3. Restart R (RStudio: Session > Restart R). R/config.R also reads this file
#    directly, so knitting and Rscript work even without a restart.
#
# `.Renviron` is git-ignored: your path never goes into the repo.
# Use forward slashes, also on Windows (C:/Users/you/...). No quotes needed.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

STAT462_DATA=/path/to/Group 8 Project/Dataset

# Optional: where cleaned tables are written. Default: <STAT462_DATA>/derived
# STAT462_DERIVED=/path/to/Group 8 Project/Dataset/derived
